menu "AJ dongle"

    config DONGLE_VIDEO_BENCH
        bool "Video relay bench: synthesise the car's stream on the dongle (bench builds only)"
        default n
        help
            With this set, a `view` datagram from the phone that carries a `"bench":<kbps>` key
            makes the video relay synthesise frames itself — 15 a second, sized to <kbps>, cut
            into 1400-byte chunks with genuine wire headers, paced one chunk per
            DONGLE_VIDEO_BENCH_PACE_US — and send them to the phone over the same socket, from
            the same task, through the same lwIP → NCM → USB path the relayed stream takes.
            Nothing reaches the car: the view is not forwarded. It measures the dongle → host
            path alone, with the same probe that measures the real stream
            (scratchpad loss_probe.py, `--bench-kbps`). A view without the key relays as usual.
            Never in a release.

    config DONGLE_VIDEO_BENCH_PACE_US
        int "Bench: microseconds between chunks"
        depends on DONGLE_VIDEO_BENCH
        default 1000
        range 0 20000
        help
            0 spreads each frame's chunks evenly over the frame period (steady load).

endmenu
